WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.820
Dissolve 2.50 grams of a
blue copper salt in water.

2
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:06.780
Some of that mass is copper.

3
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:08.920
But how much, exactly?

4
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:14.680
Yet in a flask under a burette, a dark
shade disappears with one last drop.

5
00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:19.420
So how can a shade that suddenly vanishes
measure the copper in a blue salt?

6
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:23.680
In this mission, you'll learn why the
indicator goes in only near the end,

7
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.960
and how to spot the exact end-point.

8
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.960
Then you'll work through
a copper calculation,

9
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.840
from burette reading to
percentage of copper.

10
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:36.750
Your mission: explain how a vanishing shade
can measure the copper in a blue salt.